# Build-context ignore for `docker build -f Dockerfile.release` only (CI-053).
#
# BuildKit uses `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to `.dockerignore`
# when present, and it REPLACES (does not merge) it — so this must repeat the
# global rules below. The one addition over the global .dockerignore is
# `internal/server/dist`: the release image regenerates the SPA in its
# `ui-builder` stage and copies the fresh output over `internal/server/dist`
# (Dockerfile.release), so shipping the committed copy into the context is pure
# waste (and risks a stale artifact leaking in). Other images (gh-test, shauth)
# keep the committed dist because they embed it directly without a rebuild
# stage; they use the global `.dockerignore`, which does not list it.
.git
.build
.local
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.tfvars
**/*.tfplan
**/*.pem
**/*.key
bleephub-server
bleephub-dqlite-node
web/node_modules
web/core/node_modules
web/dist
web/core/dist
web/.auth
web/test-results
web/playwright-report
web/core/e2e
web/core/src/__tests__

# Regenerated by the release image's ui-builder stage; never ship the committed copy.
internal/server/dist
